"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_restaurant_kitchen_pos_doc=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_restaurant_kitchen_pos_doc||[]).push([[430],{2367(e,t,r){r.r(t),r.d(t,{_pageData:()=>o,default:()=>a});var n=r(641);const o=JSON.parse('{"path":"/kitchen-customer-screen/order-lifecycle.html","title":"Order Lifecycle","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Order Lifecycle","description":"The five kitchen statuses, how kitchen ticket numbers are generated, how they relate to WooCommerce order numbers, and when the board clears itself."},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"kitchen-customer-screen/order-lifecycle.md"}'),s={name:"order-lifecycle.md"},a=(0,r(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,t,r,o,s,a){const i=(0,n.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[t[3]||(t[3]=(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="order-lifecycle" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#order-lifecycle"><span>Order Lifecycle</span></a></h1><p>A kitchen ticket is its own record with its own number, separate from the WooCommerce order. Knowing how the two relate saves a lot of confusion at the counter.</p><h2 id="the-five-statuses" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-five-statuses"><span>The five statuses</span></a></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Where it appears</th><th>Moved on by</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>On Hold</strong></td><td>Kitchen <strong>On Hold</strong> column, POS <strong>Kitchen Orders</strong> tab</td><td>The kitchen selecting <strong>Start</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Preparing</strong></td><td>Kitchen <strong>Preparing</strong> column, customer screen <strong>Preparing</strong> list</td><td>The kitchen selecting <strong>Mark as Completed</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Completed</strong></td><td>Kitchen <strong>Completed</strong> column, customer screen <strong>Completed</strong> list</td><td>The kitchen selecting <strong>Send</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sent</strong></td><td>POS <strong>Sent Orders</strong> tab. The ticket has left the kitchen board</td><td>The counter selecting <strong>Create Bill</strong>, or <strong>Back to Hold</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Deleted</strong></td><td>Nowhere. The ticket is gone</td><td>The counter selecting <strong>Delete</strong> on the Kitchen Orders tab</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every step can be walked back:</p><ul><li><strong>Preparing → On Hold</strong> with <strong>Back to Hold</strong> on the kitchen board;</li><li><strong>Completed → Preparing</strong> with <strong>Back to Prepare</strong> on the kitchen board;</li><li><strong>Sent → On Hold</strong> with <strong>Back to Hold</strong> on the POS Sent Orders tab.</li></ul><h2 id="dine-in-and-take-away-take-different-routes" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#dine-in-and-take-away-take-different-routes"><span>Dine in and take away take different routes</span></a></h2><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Dine in</th><th>Take away</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sent to the kitchen</td><td>Before payment, from the cart</td><td>After payment, from the payment page</td></tr><tr><td>WooCommerce order at that moment</td><td>Does not exist yet</td><td>Already created</td></tr><tr><td>Ticket card shows</td><td><em>Dine In</em> plus the table name and booking number</td><td><em>Take Away</em> plus the WooCommerce order number</td></tr><tr><td>Bill raised</td><td>Later, with <strong>Create Bill</strong> on the Sent Orders tab</td><td>Already paid</td></tr><tr><td>More items can be added</td><td>Yes, with <strong>ADD MORE</strong></td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ticket-numbers" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#ticket-numbers"><span>Ticket numbers</span></a></h2><p>Every ticket gets a short kitchen number that is easy to call across a kitchen. How it counts depends on the live channel.</p><ul><li><strong>Firebase</strong> numbers tickets per day. The number restarts each morning and begins with the day of the month, so on the 7th the first ticket of the day is <strong>#71</strong>, then #72, #73 and so on.</li><li><strong>Socket</strong> keeps one running number that never restarts. The very first ticket is numbered the same way — the day of the month followed by 1, so <strong>#211</strong> if the channel is first used on the 21st — and every ticket after that adds one, whatever the date: #212, #213 and onwards.</li></ul><p>On both channels one counter is shared by all outlets.</p><p>A take away ticket also carries the <strong>WooCommerce order number</strong> on its card, shown as <em>Take Away #219</em>. That is the number to use when looking the order up under <strong>WooCommerce → Orders</strong>. A dine in ticket has no WooCommerce number until the bill is raised.</p><h3 id="if-you-use-an-order-number-prefix" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#if-you-use-an-order-number-prefix"><span>If you use an order number prefix</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Order Id Prefix</strong> set under <strong>Restaurant POS → Settings → General</strong> is applied to the numbers shown on the kitchen tabs <em>inside</em> the Point of Sale and on the printed kitchen and thermal receipts, so a ticket reads <em>#POS_76</em> there. The standalone kitchen board shows the bare number, <em>#76</em>, and its search box matches the bare number too. Type the digits without the prefix when you look a ticket up on the board.</p><h2 id="does-the-board-clear-itself" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#does-the-board-clear-itself"><span>Does the board clear itself?</span></a></h2><p>Only on the Firebase channel. Whichever channel you use, the kitchen record is not a sales history: your sales history is in <strong>WooCommerce → Orders</strong> and in the Point of Sale reports, and is never affected.</p><h3 id="firebase-the-board-resets-every-day" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#firebase-the-board-resets-every-day"><span>Firebase: the board resets every day</span></a></h3><p>The kitchen board holds the <strong>current day</strong> only. The first time any screen connects on a new day, the previous day&#39;s tickets are cleared automatically and the ticket counter starts again.</p><p>This means:</p><ul><li>the board never fills up with yesterday&#39;s work;</li><li>a ticket left in Completed overnight will not be there in the morning.</li></ul><div class="hint-container important"><p class="hint-container-title">Important</p><p>On Firebase, finish the day&#39;s tickets before closing. Anything still on the board when the next day starts is removed, and there is no way to bring it back.</p></div><h3 id="socket-nothing-is-cleared-automatically" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#socket-nothing-is-cleared-automatically"><span>Socket: nothing is cleared automatically</span></a></h3><p>On the Socket channel tickets are stored in your WordPress database and the module never removes them by date. This means:</p><ul><li>a ticket left in On Hold, Preparing or Completed is still on the board the next morning, until the kitchen moves it on;</li><li>every ticket that has been sent stays listed on the POS <strong>Sent Orders</strong> tab;</li><li>a ticket is removed only when the counter deletes it with <strong>Delete</strong> on the <strong>Kitchen Orders</strong> tab. To remove a ticket from Sent Orders, select <strong>Back to Hold</strong> and then <strong>Delete</strong>.</li></ul><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Tips</p><p>On Socket, end each service with an empty board — send what was served and delete what was not — so the next shift starts clean.</p></div><h2 id="what-is-written-to-the-woocommerce-order" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-is-written-to-the-woocommerce-order"><span>What is written to the WooCommerce order</span></a></h2><p>For a take away order sent through the payment page checkbox, WooCommerce records that the order was sent to the kitchen. Nothing else about the order — its status, its totals, its items — is changed by this module. Order statuses, stock and reports behave exactly as they do without it.</p><h2 id="no-emails" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#no-emails"><span>No emails</span></a></h2><p>This module sends <strong>no WooCommerce email</strong>. There is no kitchen email template and no customer email about preparation. The alerts it does send are ordinary browser notifications on the kitchen board and on the POS screen, and only to a browser where the person allowed notifications.</p><h2 id="next-step" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#next-step"><span>Next step</span></a></h2>',31)),(0,n.Lk)("p",null,[t[1]||(t[1]=(0,n.eW)("If something is not behaving as described here, see ",-1)),(0,n.bF)(i,{to:"/kitchen-customer-screen/troubleshooting.html"},{default:(0,n.k6)(()=>[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,n.eW)("Troubleshooting",-1)])]),_:1}),t[2]||(t[2]=(0,n.eW)(".",-1))])])}]])}}]);